    "task": "repertoire-similarity"
  },
  "task": "There is 10x-genomics single cell CellRanger data with RNA-seq (feature bc matrix) and TCR-seq (contig annotations) data for blood (*B samples), tumor (*T samples) and normal tumor-adjascent tissue (*N samples) for different patients. Load the data, perform quality control as necessary and integrate the samples. Use only TCR data, with from one to two functional pairs of chains. Define clonotypes. Compute the Jaccard distance matrix between samples and use it to determine whether samples cluster together primarily by patient identity (write \"patient\") or by tissue type (\"tissue\"). How many clonotypes are shared between LT5 and LN5? How many distinct clonotypes appear in two or more samples? What tissue types correlate the strongest in terms of clonotype sizes? Write the tissues (e.g. \"blood x tumor\", \"blood x normal\", \"normal x tumor\") and the size of the correlation (e.g. 0.75)"
}
